          "date": "2026-11-04 01:39:42.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 lfs: add lfs migrate -m --with-data",
        "message": "LU-21061 lfs: add lfs migrate -m --with-data\n\n\"lfs migrate -m -p POOL\" moves the directories and inodes of a tree\nonto the MDTs of a pool, but the file data stays on the OSTs it was\non, and default file layouts in the tree may still name another pool,\nso new files keep going there.\n\nAdd --with-data: after the metadata, walk the tree, give POOL to each\ndefault file layout that names another pool, and migrate the data of\neach file whose OST components do not all name POOL through the \"lfs\nmigrate\" path, keeping the rest of its layout apart from OST indices.\nWith -d, only the files in the directory move.  Mirrored, released\nand busy files are reported and left in place, and rerunning the\ncommand moves them and skips what has moved already.  Nothing moves\nto a pool that lists no OSTs, and DoM data stays with its inode.\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I9ff5aa2106a3c1712d186bba72c9d9c68affae71\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
